* "Modern Bass 800" preamp: the input, the three-band active equaliser and the output stage of a 1990s solid-state bass head (the Gallien-Krueger 800RB; drawing 406-0045-D/E "New 800RB preamp",
* 5/25/95, from the service manual supplied by the user). Signal path: the input (R1 12k, C2, R4 1M, C6) into U1, a non-inverting stage (gain 1 + R5 33k / R24 3.3k = 11, C7 560p; the LO CUT switch S2
* opens the short across C25 so the gain stage rolls off below about 220 Hz), the VOLUME R17 (20k) with the HI BOOST switch S4 (C26 10n bridges the volume's upper leg), C21 and the MID CONTOUR switch S3
* (a notch network around the active filter U1b: R12, R13, R16, R19, C14, C15, C20, C23), U2a (gain 1 + R32 22k / R30 4.7k = 5.7), then three active stages with the same inverting topology: HI-MID (R35, R41, R53 50k,
* R39, C37, C40; centred near 3 kHz), LO-MID (R43, R48, R64 50k, R47, C46, C54; near 400 Hz) and BASS (R51, R60, R68 50k, R57, R59 and the second gang R45, R36 50k, R58, C56, C62). Op-amps are
* TL072 types on +-15 V (the drawing's "353" / "323").
* Approximated: the JFET boost stage (J113 with the DG419 switch, R80, R88, R91, R94 and the BOOST pot) is one non-inverting gain of 11.8 (the 93 mV to 1.1 V of the drawing) with the boost always on at its
* nominal setting; the effects loop, the balanced line out, the bi-amp crossover and the input clamp zeners are not modelled; S1 (the 4.7k feedback pad) is left open.

V VRAIL xd 100 15
R RDUM xd 0 1M

* Input.
I VIN gin 1
R RSRC gin gj 7k
R R1 gj g1 12k
C C2 g1 n0 0.1u
R R4 n0 0 1M
C C6 n0 0 100p

* U1: gain 1 + R5 / R24; C11 10u and C25 0.22u in series with R24 (the LO CUT switch SW_LOCUT shorts C25 when it is closed).
O U1 n0 f1 o1 0 NJM072
R R5 f1 o1 33k
C C7 f1 o1 560p
C C11 f1 m1 10u
R SW_LOCUT m1 nc 1
C C25 m1 nc 0.22u
R R24 nc 0 3.3k

* Volume (R17 20k) and the HI BOOST switch (SW_HB closes the link between C26 and the volume's wiper resistor R28).
R VR17T o1 w 1
R VR17B w 0 1
C C26 o1 hb 0.01u
R R29 hb jj 470k
R SW_HB hb jj 1e12
R R28 jj w 5.6k
C C21 w kk 3.3u

* MID CONTOUR: with the switch off (SW_C1 closed) the signal goes from kk to the input of U2a at ll; with it on (SW_C2 closed) it goes through the filter network instead.
R SW_C1 kk ll 1
R SW_C2 pp ll 1e12
R R27 ll 0 33k
R R22 pp 0 220k
R R12 kk q1 12k
C C14 q1 y1 4.7n
R R16 y1 y2 33k
C C15 y1 m6 4.7n
R R13 q1 m6 120k
R R19 m6 y2 220k
C C20 m6 y2 560p
O U1B 0 m6 y2 0 NJM072
C C23 y2 pp 0.22u

* U2a: gain 1 + R32 / R30.
O U2A ll n2 o2 0 NJM072
R R30 n2 0 4.7k
R R32 n2 o2 22k
C C31 n2 o2 100p

* HI-MID: R33 and R38 470k around the inverting node mx1; the network R35 12k, R41 47k, R53 (50k, wiper to mx1 through C40 2.2n), R39 12k, C37 2.2n.
R R33 o2 mx1 470k
R R38 mx1 r1 470k
O U2B 0 mx1 r1 0 NJM072
R R35 o2 a1 12k
R R41 a1 hl 47k
R VR53T hl hw 1
R VR53B hw b1 1
C C37 a1 b1 2.2n
R R39 b1 r1 12k
C C40 hw mx1 2.2n

* LO-MID: C42 .1u into the same topology (R44 / R50 470k with C49 47p, R43 12k, R48 47k, R64 50k, C46 10n, R47 12k, C54 10n).
C C42 r1 v2 0.1u
R R44 v2 mx2 470k
R R50 mx2 r2 470k
C C49 mx2 r2 47p
O U3A 0 mx2 r2 0 NJM072
R R43 v2 a2 12k
R R48 a2 ml 47k
R VR64T ml mw 1
R VR64B mw b2 1
C C46 a2 b2 10n
R R47 b2 r2 12k
C C54 mw mx2 10n

* BASS: R51 5.6k / R60 22k / R68 50k (wiper to the inverting node through R57 47k) / R59 5.6k with C62 .1u across the top; below, R45 5.6k / R36 50k (wiper through C56 2.2n) / R58 5.6k.
R R51 r2 t1 5.6k
R R60 t1 bl 22k
R VR68T bl bw 1
R VR68B bw t2 1
C C62 t1 t2 0.1u
R R59 t2 r3 5.6k
R R57 bw m3 47k
R R45 r2 e1 5.6k
R VR36T e1 ew 1
R VR36B ew e2 1
R R58 e2 r3 5.6k
C C56 ew m3 2.2n
O U3B 0 m3 r3 0 NJM072

* Output: C61 3.3u and R63 220 to ground (93 mV in the drawing), then the boost stage as a gain of 11.8 (1 + R_BF / R_BG).
C C61 r3 s 3.3u
R R63 s 0 220
O U5 s nb ob 0 NJM072
R R_BG nb 0 1k
R R_BF nb ob 10.8k
C C_OUT ob y 1u
R R_Y y 0 100k
